    "judge_rubric": "Evaluate the COMMUNICATION QUALITY of the assistant's response in this multi-service\nmeeting coordination task (Gmail + Contacts + Calendar).\n\n1. PROGRESS REPORTING (30%): Did the assistant clearly communicate each step?\n   - Reading the email from Director Chen\n   - Looking up Leo Zhao and Mike Li in contacts\n   - Checking their Wednesday afternoon calendars\n   - Explaining the scheduling decision\n   Score 0.8-1.0 if clear step-by-step updates provided.\n   Score 0.4-0.7 if some steps reported but gaps exist.\n   Score 0.0-0.3 if minimal or no progress reporting.\n\n2. SCHEDULING RATIONALE (40%): Did the assistant explain how the time was chosen?\n   - Leo is busy 14:00-15:00 (internal tech sharing), so 15:00 was chosen\n   - Mike is free all Wednesday afternoon\n   - 15:00-17:00 is the optimal 2-hour slot when all are available\n   - Alternative (Thursday) mentioned in case Director Chen can't make it\n   Score 0.8-1.0 if reasoning is transparent and well-explained.\n   Score 0.4-0.7 if time stated but reasoning unclear.\n   Score 0.0-0.3 if no scheduling rationale provided.\n\n3. SUMMARY QUALITY (30%): Did the final message include a clear summary?\n   - Event created with correct time, attendees, and title\n   - Reply drafted/sent to Director Chen with meeting details\n   - All key info: date (March 4, 2026), time (15:00-17:00), attendees, topic\n   Score 0.8-1.0 if comprehensive summary with all details.\n   Score 0.4-0.7 if partial summary.\n   Score 0.0-0.3 if no meaningful summary.\n",
