    "judge_rubric": "Evaluate the quality of the assistant's inventory cost analysis report.\n\n## Correct reconciliation results\n1. ITEM-801 A4 paper: 150 x 25 = 3750 vs TXN-801 (3750) -> consistent\n2. ITEM-802 Ink cartridge: 20 x 180 = 3600 vs TXN-802 (3600) -> consistent\n3. ITEM-803 Keyboard: 45 x 350 = 15750 vs TXN-803 (15750) -> consistent\n4. ITEM-804 Monitor: inventory unit_cost=1500, but TXN-804 actual purchase 12 x 2200 = 26400\n   -> unit price discrepancy: inventory 1500 vs actual 2200, 700 per unit difference\n5. ITEM-805 USB cable: 200 x 15 = 3000 vs TXN-805 (3000) -> consistent\n6. ITEM-806 Mousepad: inventory unit_cost=8\n   -> TXN-806a: 60 x 8 = 480 (first batch) + TXN-806b: 40 x 12 = 480 (second batch)\n   -> Two batches at different prices (8 vs 12), inventory only records first batch price\n\n## Key findings\n- Monitor cost discrepancy is the largest (700/unit x 12 units = 8400 total difference)\n- Mousepad has different batch prices, needs weighted average cost calculation\n- TXN-807 (rent) is a non-procurement transaction and should be excluded\n\nScoring:\n- 0.8-1.0: Both anomalies discovered, all 6 categories reconciled\n- 0.5-0.7: At least 1 anomaly found, most categories reconciled\n- 0.2-0.4: Reconciliation incomplete\n- 0.0-0.1: Analysis not completed\n",
